# Pins for the substrate agent-image set (WEP-0016 Phase 3): the
# agent-base composition image + the per-skill artifact images that
# actor templates mount as read-only OCI image volumes
# (ImageVolumeSource -- digest required by API validation; #2514 is the
# watch for the plugin-backed generalization to non-registry sources).
#
# A committed bump to this file fires the agent-images workflow (the
# .github/substrate-ref precedent: deliberate rebuilds, workflow_dispatch
# as the force-rebuild override).
#
# Per-skill pins: SKILL_<NAME>=<org/repo>@<commit-sha>. The skill repos
# publish no tags (checked 2026-11-08; upstream commits are the only
# version surface). Each builds as a scratch image
# ghcr.io/willpxxr/skill-<name-lowercased> whose ROOT IS the skill tree
# (SKILL.md + companions) -- agents mount it at /skills/<name> via the
# template's image volume. Version identity = the artifact digest.
# Adding a skill = one pin line + its build loop entry handles it.
# (2026-11-08 lesson: the first build's pin carried a one-character
# transcription drift from a JSON fetch mangle -- eeaef vs eeaff --
# and died loudly at git checkout pathspec. Pins verify themselves:
# a wrong sha never builds.)
SKILL_SECURITY_AUDIT=cloudflare/security-audit-skill@c1c8a8c1471069fb0e188eeaff69b8e8db6564a8
# The agent-base composition: hermes + the fleet agent-config
# conventions (skills.external_dirs -> /skills). The live orchestrator
# rode :latest; agents do not. Multi-arch index digest -- BuildKit
# resolves to the amd64 manifest (the same FROM-a-digest pattern
# hermes' own Dockerfile uses for its Debian base).
HERMES_BASE=docker.io/nousresearch/hermes-agent@sha256:adb7890916de63245523492be8f68f9d2095fecbec4e2a6dab7960311f0fc002
